# Files that may name the GitHub owner, one path per line. None should need
# to: workflows read it from GitHub's own context, and the agentv package gets
# its update address written in when CI builds it. Moving the repos to an
# organisation then changes no code (HANDOFF.md, "No GitHub owner in code").
# Markdown is never scanned for it, so READMEs can link the repos.

# GitHub's Sponsor button reads a Sponsors account by its name here. It names
# the person, not where the repos live, so a move to an organisation keeps it.
.github/FUNDING.yml
